WEBVTT

00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:06.560
<i>Listen. We'll make a pincer attack on the Diva.</i>

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:11.030
<i>The plan is to attack from two directions at once, and draw out our prey.</i>

00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:14.360
Zanald's in too much of a hurry for glory.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:18.370
I won't let you get away, Gundam!

00:00:19.450 --> 00:00:21.290
Former Commander Asuno, where are you going?

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:23.750
The enemy's trying to capture the Gundam!

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:24.790
I'm going out too!

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:31.420
At this rate, I won't make it!

00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:34.550
You thought I'd be easier to defeat?

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:40.520
There are more ways to attack than just beams and swords!{lol so what exactly did that even do??}

00:00:58.240 --> 00:00:59.870
You're coming with me.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:11.960
I won't let you take Kio!

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:17.430
The Mars settlement plan.

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:22.350
The people left behind in the Mars Sphere in the wake of its failure

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.890
formed the independent nation of Vagan,

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:29.060
and launched a war against the Earth Federation government.

00:01:30.860 --> 00:01:33.320
70 years have already passed

00:01:33.320 --> 00:01:39.410
since the conflict began.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:47.000
todokasete kono mune ni

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:47.000
Let your voice reach my heart

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.500
kasuka ni nokoru kimi no koe wo

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:50.500
though it lingers but faintly in the air

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:53.920
yume ja nai genjitsu de

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:53.920
In a world that I know is not a dream

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:59.680
samayoitsuzuketeita

00:01:53.920 --> 00:01:59.680
I kept wandering

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:11.440
tachidomaru no mo mae ni susumu koto mo

00:02:08.140 --> 00:02:11.440
Halting in your tracks and walking ahead proudly

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:14.900
atozusari na ki ga shiteta

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:14.900
both seemed too fearsome a choice

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:18.360
tojikomerareta shikakui sora no shita

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:18.360
Here on the board, where we are bound to

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:21.620
iki wo hisometeta

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:21.620
I tried to breathe softly to blend in

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:29.040
tsumetai hoho wo tsutawaru kako no yowasa nugutte

00:02:21.620 --> 00:02:29.040
I swept away the weakness of the past trailing down my cheeks

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:35.510
hikari sasu basho he kono te wo nobasu yo

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:35.510
and held out my hands to the light

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:41.090
todokasete kono mune ni

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:41.090
Let your voice reach my heart

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:44.600
kasuka ni nokoru kimi no koe wo

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:44.600
though it lingers but faintly in the air

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:48.020
yume ja nai genjitsu de

00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:48.020
In a world that I know is not a dream

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:50.980
sagashitsuzuketeru

00:02:48.020 --> 00:02:50.980
I kept searching

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:55.110
todokaseru sono mune ni

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:55.110
I will let my feelings and my voice

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:58.530
tashika na omoi boku no koe wo

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:58.530
reach your heart

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:01.950
owaranai genjitsu de

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:01.950
Through days without end

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:05.370
sakebitsuzuketeiku

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:05.370
I will be proud, be strong

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:11.210
ashita wo shinjite

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:11.210
and have faith in the future

00:03:13.880 --> 00:03:19.260
Episode 36
 Stolen Gundam

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:22.930
What?

00:03:22.930 --> 00:03:24.550
A Gundam!

00:03:24.550 --> 00:03:25.850
Is it Flit Asuno?

00:03:27.770 --> 00:03:28.680
Grandpa!

00:03:29.770 --> 00:03:31.190
Run, Kio!

00:03:31.190 --> 00:03:33.100
I'll take care of these guys!

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:34.520
But...!

00:03:34.520 --> 00:03:36.900
I can't leave you out here alone!

00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.650
<i>You don't have to worry about me!</i>

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:42.200
<i>Just concentrate on getting away!</i>

00:03:45.280 --> 00:03:46.780
<i>Kio!</i>

00:03:49.200 --> 00:03:50.870
No, you don't!

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:56.250
I'll leave this to you.

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:58.340
I'll chase the other Gundam.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:01.170
What?

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:11.480
<i>I'm</i>  your opponent!{i am your opponernt!}

00:04:23.490 --> 00:04:26.280
Damage to port side section 6!

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.830
Checking extent of damage!

00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:30.910
The rear enemy ship is accelerating towards us.

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:32.080
How's the photon blaster?

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:34.960
Energy charge is at 55%!

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:38.750
Once it's charged, fire the photon blaster to open a path,

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:41.630
and leave this sector at full combat speed!

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:44.380
What are the mobile suits doing?

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:47.390
All Abis team units are fighting near the Diva.

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:49.810
Gundam AGE-3 is now returning,

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:54.730
but Former Commander Asuno's AGE-1 is pretty far ahead of us.

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:57.940
Sergeant Major Carl, tell him to withdraw!

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:06.660
<i>Former Commander Asuno!</i>

00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:09.780
<i>After we fire the photon blaster, we're leaving this sector.</i>

00:05:09.780 --> 00:05:10.910
<i>Please come back!</i>

00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:12.120
What about Kio—

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:13.540
What about the AGE-3?

00:05:13.540 --> 00:05:15.210
<i>It's currently returning to ship.</i>

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:16.960
<i>It should be landing soon.</i>

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:21.380
Okay. Once you've recovered the AGE-3, the Diva will depart immediately.

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:24.760
I'll continue to hold off the enemy attack here!

00:05:24.760 --> 00:05:28.300
<i>What? You're going to stay there by yourself?!</i>

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:30.560
<i>I'll make sure the AGE-3 escapes!</i>

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:32.520
<i>Don't worry about me!</i>

00:05:32.520 --> 00:05:33.220
Grandpa!

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:37.940
Kio!

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:39.650
<i>Kio has reversed course!</i>

00:05:39.650 --> 00:05:41.980
<i>He's heading out to help the former commander!</i>

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:43.150
That's...{herp derp}{that's.. or whatever}

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:48.410
Mr. Obright, I'm leaving this up to you.

00:05:48.410 --> 00:05:49.530
Stop Kio!

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:50.450
<i>Roger that.</i>

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.580
Derek, keep protecting the Diva.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:56.040
Hang on until Kio and the former commander are back!

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:56.500
<i>Roger!</i>

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:59.420
<i>Is this acceptable for the mobile suit team, Captain?</i>

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:00.040
Yes!

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:03.920
Photon blaster energy charge at 72%!

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:23.770
Damn! So you're determined to get in our way, huh?{ You'll stand in our way no matter what, huh?}

00:06:23.770 --> 00:06:28.610
<i>Calm down. If we take our time and keep attacking, he'll come back.</i>

00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:29.530
What?

00:06:31.450 --> 00:06:33.030
I can tell.

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:37.040
Grandpa!

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:40.460
You won't just let him die.

00:06:42.380 --> 00:06:43.290
Here he is!

00:06:48.880 --> 00:06:51.010
Kio! Why did you come back?

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:53.510
<i>You can't stay behind by yourself!</i>

00:06:59.230 --> 00:07:00.980
Gundam! I'm going to capture you!{gotta catch'em all, pokemon!}{getto da ze}

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:06.440
I see. You were right.

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:08.650
I guess I underestimated you a little.

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:11.610
I won't let you hurt Grandpa!

00:07:12.110 --> 00:07:14.280
So you had the nerve to come back!

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:41.390
You won't get away this time!{RAPE RAPE RAPE RAPE}

00:07:46.730 --> 00:07:47.900
Come on!

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:51.280
<i>Resistance is futile!{Stop this useless resistance!}</i>

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:56.830
If you keep struggling, I'll take more than an arm next time!

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:00.040
N-No...

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:10.880
Kio!

00:08:12.760 --> 00:08:16.550
I can't defend myself while holding the Gundam.

00:08:16.550 --> 00:08:18.680
You'll have to assist me, Zeheart!

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:26.520
Zanald, you bastard!

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:30.690
Distract the enemy until I get back to my ship!

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:31.860
Wait!

00:08:38.160 --> 00:08:44.540
<i>Whatever. Our goal was to bring that Gundam to Lord Ezelcant.</i>

00:08:51.380 --> 00:08:52.800
Kio!

00:09:04.190 --> 00:09:06.190
AGE-3 has been captured!

00:09:06.190 --> 00:09:08.560
They're heading for the ship behind the Diva!

00:09:08.940 --> 00:09:12.690
Turn around 180 degrees! Stop them with the photon blaster!

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:13.940
<i>Didn't you hear me?</i>

00:09:13.940 --> 00:09:16.280
<i>Turn the Diva around 180 degrees!</i>

00:09:16.280 --> 00:09:17.280
That's crazy!

00:09:17.280 --> 00:09:20.370
If we turn around here, the enemy in front will shoot us!

00:09:20.370 --> 00:09:24.120
Photon blaster energy charge at 90%!

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:26.670
If we're going to break through, this is our only chance!

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:28.880
If we turn around here...

00:09:29.590 --> 00:09:32.510
<i>Are you going to hand over the AGE-3 to the enemy?!</i>

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:35.260
<i>Follow my orders, Captain!</i>

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:36.930
B-But...

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:38.340
Captain...

00:09:57.910 --> 00:09:59.780
Looks like they're planning something.{my common sense is tingling...}

00:10:00.280 --> 00:10:02.410
In that case, I shouldn't linger here.

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:19.090
An attack from the Fa Zard?

00:10:19.090 --> 00:10:20.550
Good timing, Fram!

00:10:31.060 --> 00:10:33.320
The enemy ship in front of us has changed course!

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:35.150
Could they be withdrawing?

00:10:36.530 --> 00:10:38.320
Same with the ship behind us!

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:42.490
They're getting out of photon blaster effective range!

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:44.240
Resetting aim...

00:10:45.700 --> 00:10:46.660
There's not enough time!

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:54.500
They've stolen the Gundam!

00:11:02.430 --> 00:11:05.180
Kio!

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:17.480
Why didn't you turn around when I said so?!

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:21.860
If you had, we could've recovered the AGE-3!

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:26.790
Exposing the ship's flank would've been suicidal.

00:11:26.790 --> 00:11:29.290
We'd be inviting the enemy in front to attack us.

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:32.880
I understand your feelings, but...

00:11:32.880 --> 00:11:37.420
Former Commander, right now you're missing your usual composure.

00:11:37.420 --> 00:11:38.880
What did you say?!

00:11:56.110 --> 00:11:59.150
I know I said that to the former commander,

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:02.610
but I wanted to go after Kio, too.

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:05.950
The ship has taken heavy damage, though.

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:08.370
We need to resupply, as well.

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:10.910
It's impossible for us to pursue them right now.

00:12:10.910 --> 00:12:13.040
Resupply, huh?

00:12:13.040 --> 00:12:16.750
But there are no colonies around here, let alone a supply base...

00:12:16.750 --> 00:12:21.720
Then why not request help from a civilian factory ship?

00:12:21.720 --> 00:12:26.350
Given our present course, there's one we can rendezvous with in two or three days.

00:12:26.350 --> 00:12:29.260
A factory ship in the middle of a war zone?

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:33.190
Is it perhaps the Madorna Workshop?

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:33.980
Yes.

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:36.480
I see. That's perfect, but...

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:38.690
I wonder what Mr. Rody will say.

00:12:38.690 --> 00:12:41.530
For now, I'll try to make contact.

00:12:41.530 --> 00:12:44.030
Captain, is that okay?

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:46.280
Y-Yes. Please do.

00:13:00.500 --> 00:13:01.880
Lt. Commander Abis...

00:13:02.300 --> 00:13:05.050
You made the right decision, Captain.

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:08.800
We're all worried about Kio, but don't let it bother you too much.

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:13.810
I couldn't make <i>any</i>  decisions.

00:13:13.810 --> 00:13:16.270
I just fumbled and hesitated...

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:20.360
But you didn't follow the former commander's orders right away

00:13:20.360 --> 00:13:24.240
because you had doubts about them, right?

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:26.860
Of course you hesitated.

00:13:26.860 --> 00:13:28.990
All of our lives were in the balance.

00:13:30.030 --> 00:13:31.160
Don't worry.

00:13:31.870 --> 00:13:34.200
You're becoming a fine captain.

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:42.840
I'm not telling you to get it back into perfect shape!

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:46.050
I just need you to get it to move!

00:13:46.050 --> 00:13:49.470
B-But we've already got our hands full.

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:52.600
And you call yourself a mechanic?!

00:13:52.600 --> 00:13:54.980
Please wait, Former Commander Asuno.

00:13:54.980 --> 00:13:57.640
We don't have enough materials nor manpower right now.

00:13:57.640 --> 00:14:01.940
If we don't make triage decisions on repairs, we'll never get anything done. {order of priorty for damage extent and whats most important to get fixed first}

00:14:01.940 --> 00:14:06.490
And the AGE-1 is the most badly damaged of all.

00:14:06.490 --> 00:14:08.950
Then I'll repair it myself.

00:14:08.950 --> 00:14:10.410
I don't need any help.

00:14:10.410 --> 00:14:13.370
I'm the only worker I need!

00:14:13.950 --> 00:14:17.790
Even if we get one machine working, could we pursue them right away?

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:20.830
So you want me to sit here and do nothing?!

00:14:20.830 --> 00:14:22.380
Flit...{removing the Mr. because >first name}

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:25.760
Dad.

00:14:26.380 --> 00:14:27.340
Unoa.

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:28.930
What's wrong?

00:14:28.930 --> 00:14:32.430
It's not like you to get so emotional.

00:14:32.930 --> 00:14:35.850
I'm not emotional at all!

00:14:36.430 --> 00:14:37.640
You're lying.

00:14:37.640 --> 00:14:40.900
You're really just worried about Kio, aren't you?

00:14:44.110 --> 00:14:48.780
Kio's talents were rapidly emerging as he piloted the Gundam.

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:52.950
He could have become the savior that defeated the Vagan!

00:14:52.950 --> 00:14:55.830
And he was taken from us before our very eyes!

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:58.040
Don't try to cover it up with reasoning.

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:00.120
We all understand how you feel.

00:15:00.120 --> 00:15:02.290
Just be honest about it!

00:15:22.350 --> 00:15:23.770
Flit...

00:15:29.070 --> 00:15:30.610
Wait, you guys!

00:15:30.610 --> 00:15:34.160
I told you, this place is off-limits!

00:15:34.160 --> 00:15:36.160
Off-limits! Off-limits!

00:15:36.160 --> 00:15:37.450
No!

00:15:37.450 --> 00:15:40.040
They said they don't have enough people!

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:42.170
I'm gonna help!

00:15:42.170 --> 00:15:43.080
Me too!

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:43.580
Me too!

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:46.670
Hey, hey, this isn't a playground!

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:47.670
Sorry!

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:50.090
Come on, you guys!

00:15:49.550 --> 00:15:51.130
Off-limits! Off-limits!

00:15:50.090 --> 00:15:51.130
Don't wanna!

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:52.300
Get back here!

00:15:52.180 --> 00:15:53.260
Yeah. {flit's grunt}

00:15:52.720 --> 00:15:53.550
Hey now!

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:55.680
Gotcha!

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:56.760
No!

00:15:57.930 --> 00:16:02.690
Listen. This is an important job. It's not a game!

00:16:02.690 --> 00:16:03.650
Right!

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:05.150
Roger that, ma'am!

00:16:11.400 --> 00:16:12.910
You're so strong.

00:16:12.910 --> 00:16:14.620
Huh? What?

00:16:14.620 --> 00:16:15.870
You're strong.

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:17.280
What do you mean?

00:16:17.280 --> 00:16:19.660
Aren't you worried about Kio?

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:21.250
You're old friends, right?

00:16:21.870 --> 00:16:24.500
Kio will definitely be back.

00:16:24.920 --> 00:16:28.420
I don't know how, but I can tell.

00:16:30.050 --> 00:16:31.420
I see...

00:16:31.970 --> 00:16:34.090
You guys are amazing.

00:16:34.090 --> 00:16:35.260
Really?

00:16:52.900 --> 00:16:55.450
Zanald won the glory this time.

00:16:58.120 --> 00:16:59.370
Master Zeheart...

00:17:00.330 --> 00:17:02.080
I heard from the soldiers

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:06.710
that Master Zanald got the Gundam by pushing you around.

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:11.380
The Gundam was successfully captured. That's all that matters.

00:17:11.380 --> 00:17:12.260
But—

00:17:12.260 --> 00:17:15.550
More importantly, how much damage did our ship take?

00:17:18.720 --> 00:17:23.180
We're still waiting for a full casualty count.

00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:24.560
Hurry.

00:17:24.560 --> 00:17:27.060
I need to get a report from Leil too.

00:17:27.060 --> 00:17:31.610
We'll return to La Gramis and wait for Lord Ezelcant's orders.

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:32.780
Yes, sir!

00:17:37.610 --> 00:17:43.080
The covering fire you ordered when we withdrew from the combat zone was perfect.

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:44.750
Well done.

00:18:03.770 --> 00:18:05.730
The Diva crew are coming in.

00:18:05.730 --> 00:18:07.100
Screen off.

00:18:07.100 --> 00:18:07.770
Roger.

00:18:10.810 --> 00:18:12.190
Ms. Laraparly.

00:18:12.650 --> 00:18:15.280
It's been a long time, Flit Asuno!

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:18.240
To think we've both managed to survive this long!

00:18:26.750 --> 00:18:29.620
It's been a while, Mom.

00:18:35.010 --> 00:18:37.300
Hey, wait a...

00:18:37.970 --> 00:18:39.510
Mom!

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:44.140
You left home, abandoned the family business, and still think you can call me "Mom"?!{left and abandoned?}

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:45.220
You worthless son!

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:50.440
I just wanted... to improve myself!

00:18:51.900 --> 00:18:56.030
Then I can expect to see some new tricks, huh?

00:18:56.030 --> 00:18:57.990
Well, is he useful?

00:18:57.990 --> 00:19:00.160
Yes. He's an excellent engineer.

00:19:01.030 --> 00:19:03.580
I see. Then fine.

00:19:06.330 --> 00:19:07.290
Emergency call.

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:13.040
I hate to rush you, but we don't have much time.

00:19:13.040 --> 00:19:15.050
I'd like to discuss the work that's—

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:16.050
Stop!

00:19:17.210 --> 00:19:20.930
Before that, there's an emergency call for you.

00:19:20.930 --> 00:19:22.550
Answer that first.

00:19:23.010 --> 00:19:25.140
A call for me?

00:19:25.640 --> 00:19:30.940
<i>It really has been a while since we've talked like this, Father.</i>

00:19:32.690 --> 00:19:33.650
Asemu!

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:39.610
You dare show your face to me after all this time?

00:19:41.490 --> 00:19:44.990
<i>We've received information that Kio was captured by Vagan.</i>

00:19:44.990 --> 00:19:47.910
<i>We're prepared to go rescue him.</i>

00:19:49.040 --> 00:19:52.080
<i>You're not officially a soldier any more.</i>

00:19:52.080 --> 00:19:53.580
<i>It would take some time</i>

00:19:53.580 --> 00:19:57.710
<i>to mobilize a force and prepare a rescue mission.</i>

00:19:58.090 --> 00:20:01.880
<i>Whereas we can head out right away.</i>

00:20:02.510 --> 00:20:05.390
<i>Would you leave Kio to me?</i>

00:20:05.390 --> 00:20:06.810
You're joking!

00:20:06.810 --> 00:20:09.560
You're a pirate now! How can I trust you?!

00:20:11.180 --> 00:20:12.730
For whatever reason,

00:20:13.100 --> 00:20:16.650
you fled the military and betrayed your family!

00:20:25.660 --> 00:20:29.040
I don't know about your family circumstances,

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:34.210
but when it comes to rescuing this Kio kid, isn't your son right?

00:20:34.210 --> 00:20:37.920
Anybody who can act right away should do so.

00:20:38.920 --> 00:20:42.340
<i>Before Kio is your grandson, he is my child.</i>

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:48.180
<i>Let me go!{quivering eyes}{remind me why asemu needs his father's permission to do anything}{still has that complex, i guess}</i>

00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:03.280
<i>{Grand Esteemed}Father!</i>

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:09.780
Take the Gundam's spare parts.

00:21:10.330 --> 00:21:12.160
You can use them during the rescue.

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:15.540
<i>Okay, understood!</i>

00:21:15.540 --> 00:21:18.210
<i>We'll prepare to receive them at once!</i>

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:19.920
<i>To the Madorna factory ship!</i>

00:21:19.920 --> 00:21:20.710
<i>Hurry!</i>

00:21:22.210 --> 00:21:24.260
Rody. Get ready.

00:21:24.260 --> 00:21:25.300
Right!

00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:41.020
Get those parts loaded within 30 minutes.

00:21:41.020 --> 00:21:42.980
We'll begin the pursuit right after that!

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:43.610
Yes, sir!

00:21:44.490 --> 00:21:47.530
<i>Kio, hang on just a little longer.</i>

00:21:47.530 --> 00:21:49.910
<i>I'll bring you back...</i>

